Z||000000||Phantom Rage||06-02-2000||07:54 PM||||What happens when, a turbo charged duke goes into boost and you attached a 2-Bar Map sensor to the motor?  <P>Does the map sensor send a higher voltage to the computer and fry it? Given that, that is how the map sensor even works (higher voltage part.)  <BR> <BR>Will the computer know what to do with this newfound info? <P>Please, no "why turbo a duke." I just need these three questions answered.  <BR> <BR>                               Thank You <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Sillhouette.com||06-03-2000||01:49 AM||||I think it's a great idea to turbo your 2.5.  As for your answer.  It all depends on how much boost you are going to run into the intake.  You have to make a PROM for your computer and use the 2 bar MAP sensor.  I don't know what injector is used on the 2.5 but most common problems with turbos is not enough fuel for the added air.  This might include a higher volume fuel pump with a fuel pressure riser and a high flow injector.  <P>Hope this helps.    Later<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||06-03-2000||01:51 AM||||The L4 code doesn't support a 2 Bar map, only the V6 does. At least I've found no indication in the code that it does. ||||reg||1
